%% Topic 7 answers — examiner's-eye box; included by T7QA and the compiled QA volume.

::: eye | Topic 7 rewards a five-part frame
Every violence question in this topic asks for two or three things at once — define, explain forms, devise strategies, identify causes, describe consequences. Notice how each answer below uses the same five-part frame: (1) a precise **definition** (DEVAW ==1993==; the Punjab Act ==2016==); (2) current **data** — PDHS 2017–18 (**28%**), SSDO 2024 (**32,617** cases; conviction about **0.5%**), HRCP 2024 (**405** honour killings); (3) **theory** — power and control, Galtung, the ecological model; (4) the **forms, causes, laws or consequences** the question names; and (5) **strategies** organised as prevention, protection, prosecution, provision and partnership. The three near repeats — 2016, 2017 and 2023 — are answered separately to show how to re-cut the same knowledge for "sites", "workable" and "practical". The case studies are always **analysed**, not just narrated.
:::
